Requirements: 6   with obligations: 6

[task-01] Every run that calls a model reports what it spent, not only `acceptance
    check` and `acceptance decompose`. The benchmark's command-line runs — the
    instability measurement and the mutant audit — print the same per-stage usage table
    when they finish, with live and replayed calls counted apart, so a large offline run
    shows what it cost.
    -> every-model-run-reports-spend  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Every run that calls a model reports what it spent on completion, regardless of
       which command or entry point issued the call, and not only for `acceptance check`
       and `acceptance decompose`.
    -> check-decompose-keep-reporting-spend  [regression/inferred, code_and_tests]
       Preserve the existing spend reporting of `acceptance check` and `acceptance
       decompose` while extending it to every other run that calls a model.
    -> benchmark-cli-prints-usage-table  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       When the benchmark's instability measurement command-line run finishes, it prints
       the same per-stage usage table that `acceptance check` and `acceptance decompose`
       print.
    -> mutant-audit-prints-usage-table  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       When the benchmark's mutant audit command-line run finishes, it prints the same
       per-stage usage table that `acceptance check` and `acceptance decompose` print.
    -> usage-table-live-replayed-counted-apart  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The per-stage usage table printed by the benchmark's command-line runs (the
       instability measurement and the mutant audit) counts live model calls and
       replayed calls separately, so that the two are reported apart rather than merged
       into a single count.

[task-02] The table shows what the run spent on Claude models separately from what it
    spent on any other provider, so the Claude credits a run consumed can be read off as
    a figure of its own. A call sent through the Message Batches API counts at the price
    it was billed at.
    -> claude-spend-separate-figure  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The table presents the run's spend on Claude models as a figure separate from the
       run's spend on any other provider, so the Claude credits consumed by a run can be
       read off as its own figure.
    -> batch-call-counted-at-billed-price  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       A call sent through the Message Batches API is counted in the run's spend at the
       price it was billed at (the batch price), not at the standard non-batch price for
       the same model.

[task-03] Spend stays out of the review state and the rendered report, as it is today.
    -> spend-excluded-from-review-state-and-report  [invariant/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Keep spend data absent from both the review state and the rendered report, as it
       is today; the review state and the rendered report contain no spend information.

